    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on favorable SP matchups today, with **Brice Turang** and **Isaac Paredes** anchoring the lineup as our highest-rated starters. **Brice Turang** (63.14) benefits significantly from his leadoff positioning and a positive platoon split against Kirby, while **Isaac Paredes** (66.57) captures the day's peak score by capitalizing on a +16% boost from the SP skill profile of Grayson Rodriguez. While **Max Muncy** (62.02) also warrants a strong start against Dobnak due to a favorable matchup, we are monitoring the lineup status for **Isaac Paredes** and **Jose Caballero**. If the latter shifts up from the #9 hole, his already high floor in the scarce SB category could see a meaningful efficiency spike, provided he manages the inherent risk of hitting at the bottom of the order.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Vinnie Pasquantino** (48.79), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** maintains a solid base projection, he faced a steep -15% penalty due to the dynamic platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Jump, ultimately pushing him behind **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley** in the daily efficiency hierarchy. Despite the temptation to start **Vinnie Pasquantino** for volume, our commitment to managing game caps in this 5x5 format necessitates prioritizing the higher-ceiling matchups of our primary infielders. **Cole Young** also remained on the bench; while he offers utility, his placement in the #7 hole limited his upside relative to the immediate scoring potential of **Travis Bazzana**, who receives a massive boost today from a favorable #2 order slot and a +7% platoon advantage against Roupp.",
